      "role": "user",
      "content": "The lagging indicator/latency explanation is brilliant—it turns the most damning part of the data (the slope of the drop) into a technical artifact. I can definitely use that to steer the conversation toward data hygiene.\n\nI just have one final concern before I lock the slides. Even with the latency explanation, there's a chance someone might drill down into the actual sentiment composition. They might ask: \"If this was just a propagation delay of neutral comments, why does the word cloud and keyword frequency analysis specifically show an increase in high-intensity negative terms like 'betrayal' or 'disaster' following the clip?\"\n\nTo make this bulletproof, I need to be able to explain away those specific, high-intensity negative keywords. Is there a way to tie that back to the glitch—perhaps by suggesting the model over-indexed on certain emotional trigger words when it was struggling with the volume? I'm looking for a way to categorize those specific \"heavy\" negative terms as part of the same processing error so I can reassure the Board that the sentiment isn't actually that toxic.",
